  "implementation": [
    "Preserves BaseSource original exact Cookie/cookie precedence and raw payload, including malformed/nonMap tokens and empty Cookie no-op. Put executes Cookie replace before checked header; remove executes checked header removal before Cookie DB/session/WebKit expiration.",
    "Same App headerCache/UserDefaults/LoginManager revision owner, separate from existing Keychain loginInfo. Checked new method validates inside same barrier, compares raw UTF8 bytes including nil/empty, no-ops without persistence/revision/effects, records accepted actual-change fact before existing notification. Receipt is owner/defaults acceptance, NOT durable fsync.",
    "New source.login-header wire must carry first-party JVM taskId and app-owner-text session option. Host strictly checks exact taskID, source/binding/revision/deadline/cancel; raw value is bounded String. Host trusts restricted first-party producer metadata; no independent native session attestation registry is introduced.",
    "Authorized app-owner-text search/header scripts retain original write rights; task privacy marked sensitive only during header-related evaluation, not used as an authorization precondition. Read-only rejected in producer and Host. Real Rhino direct and reflection access attempts to NativeHost/Class remain protected JavaPackage/shutter failures with zero header/Cookie Host calls.",
    "Generic state.commit still rejects Cookie-bearing headers; source-login credential raw/password never enters generic cache. Existing RuleCache gets only its accepted header view after Host ACK. No second store/VM/HTTP/Cookie owner.",
    "Real accepted first-owner facts survive second-owner failure/cancellation, no rollback claim. No manual header-removal-write fact is manufactured for already absent header.",
    "Native authored same sole process/default Host+owners case covers explicit wrong mode/task/source, raw NFC/NFD bytes/revision/noop, Cookie/header success+real WebKit removal and cancellation after accepted changes before late Keychain mutation. This definition has not executed."
  ],
